==========
1. Purpose
==========

GRHayLID provides several simple initial data (ID) setups for GR(M)HD systems
using the General Relativistic Hydrodynamic Library (GRHayL). This includes

1) all five Balsara tests (simple/hybrid EOS only)
2) static equilibrium (simple/hybrid EOS only)
3) shock tube (simple/hybrid EOS only)
4) sound wave (simple/hybrid EOS only)
5) isotropic gas (tabulated EOS only)
6) constant density sphere (tabulated EOS only)

All native test setups require Cartesian coordinates and an identity spatial
metric supplied by ADMBase before HydroBase_Initial. The initializer checks the
metric at every point. Sphere interior velocities must be finite and strictly
subluminal. GRHayLID and its GRHayLib interface require REAL_PRECISION=8.

Magnetic initialization is optional for HydroTest1D. When enabled, both
HydroBase::initial_Avec and HydroBase::initial_Bvec must be "GRHayLID"; disabling
it requires another owner or no GRHayLID magnetic selectors. Both A and B are
written, with component-specific +1/2 transverse-cell offsets for A when
stagger_A_fields=yes (the default). B remains at base coordinates. These Balsara
coefficients are already normalized for GRHayL: when importing into
IllinoisGRMHD, set IllinoisGRMHD::rescale_magnetics=no. The legacy converter
convention and default are unchanged.

HydroTest1D supports Simple and Hybrid. Hybrid energy uses the cold-plus-thermal
helper and rejects benchmark pressures below the cold curve. The "sound wave"
setup is a sinusoidal longitudinal velocity perturbation on rho=P=1, rather
than a pure traveling acoustic eigenmode. Its finite amplitude must be in
[0,1), and shock_direction selects x, y, or z.

IsotropicGas and ConstantDensitySphere require Tabulated EOS and both
HydroBase::initial_Y_e=HydroBase::initial_temperature="GRHayLID". Requested
primitive triples must be finite and within effective EOS bounds. EOS errors
are diagnosed before grid publication.

The standalone operations also support another hydro producer, provided it
initializes all required inputs in HydroBase_Initial. Selecting storage does
not establish initialized data. A selector without an available GRHayLID
producer is rejected by the parameter check.

Beta equilibrium is controlled by impose_beta_equilibrium=yes and requires
Tabulated EOS. It allocates Ye/temperature even when their selectors are none,
and intentionally replaces those fields after HydroBase_Initial. It solves
mu_e-mu_n+mu_p=0 at each actual density and beq_temperature, within effective
Ye/T/rho bounds, with an absolute MeV residual tolerance controlled by
beq_residual_tolerance (default 1e-8). Exact/tolerance-qualified node roots are
accepted; a missing root or failed lookup is diagnosed. If several roots
exist, the lowest-Ye root is chosen. Base chemical potentials are used instead
of the potentially shifted munu dataset. This requires trustworthy table
chemical-potential conventions; it does not certify table provenance. Points
with rho<=1.01*rho_atm are reset to the complete EOS atmosphere, including rho,
and are deliberately exempt from the beta-equilibrium requirement.

Entropy is selected with HydroBase::initial_entropy="GRHayLID", independently
of the hydro family, and runs after beta equilibrium and before primitive to
conservative initialization. Tabulated entropy requires initialized finite
rho/Ye/T. Without beta it clamps these inputs to effective EOS bounds and
replaces rho, Ye, T, pressure, epsilon, and entropy consistently after a
successful lookup. With beta enabled it preserves rho/Ye/T and rejects
out-of-bounds states instead of clipping away equilibrium.

For Simple/Hybrid, entropy is the GRHayL native proxy P/rho^(Gamma_piece-1),
not HydroBase physical specific entropy in k_b/baryon. This route requires
allow_native_entropy_proxy=yes as an explicit agreement that every entropy
consumer expects that proxy. Generic physical-entropy consumers must not use
this setting. Density must be positive and finite and pressure nonnegative
and finite; zero-density or nonfinite inputs are rejected before evaluation.

GRHayLID does not initialize HydroBase::w_lorentz. A consumer of that field must
arrange its own metric-consistent producer and order it before the consumer.
No configured Cactus build/runtime or production-table validation is included
in this checkout; the declarations above do not establish those results.
